## 4. User Stories

Format: *As a [user], I want [action], so that [benefit].*

### Authentication & Onboarding
- As a new user, I want to sign up and log in securely, so that my data is private and persistent.
  - **Acceptance criteria:** Email/password or OAuth sign-up; session persists across browser reloads; incorrect credentials show a clear error; passwords are never stored in plaintext.
- As a user, I want to connect my GitHub account, so that SkillGap can analyze my repositories as evidence.
  - **Acceptance criteria:** GitHub OAuth consent screen clearly lists requested scopes; user can disconnect GitHub at any time; disconnecting stops further repository syncing.

### Target Job Management
- As a user, I want to create a target job with a title, company, and job description, so that SkillGap can analyze what it requires.
  - **Acceptance criteria:** Title and job description are required; company and deadline are optional; job is saved and appears in "My Targets."
- As a user, I want to save multiple target jobs, so that I can compare readiness across roles.
  - **Acceptance criteria:** User can create, view, edit, archive, and delete targets; each target has an independent roadmap and readiness score.

### Job Description Analysis
- As a user, I want the system to extract required and preferred skills from a pasted job description, so that I don't have to manually identify them.
  - **Acceptance criteria:** Extraction returns a structured list of skills grouped by category with an importance flag (required/preferred) and seniority indicators; extraction completes within a bounded time or shows a clear loading/error state.

### Resume & Profile Import
- As a user, I want to upload my resume as a PDF, so that SkillGap can extract my skills, projects, and experience.
  - **Acceptance criteria:** Accepts PDF up to a defined size limit; extracted skills/projects are shown to the user for review before being saved; user can manually correct extracted data.
- As a user, I want to manually add or edit skills, so that I can correct AI extraction mistakes.
  - **Acceptance criteria:** Manual skill edits are marked with `source = manual` and are preserved across re-syncs.

### Skill Gap Analysis
- As a user, I want to see each required skill's status (Strong/Partial/Claimed-Unproven/Missing/Low Priority), so that I know exactly where I stand.
  - **Acceptance criteria:** Every skill in the target's requirement list has exactly one status; status is explainable (user can see why it was assigned that status).
- As a user, I want to see the evidence behind each skill status, so that I trust the assessment.
  - **Acceptance criteria:** Each skill detail page lists evidence items with source type, source URL (if applicable), and evidence level (0–5).

### Roadmap & Projects
- As a user, I want a personalized roadmap of tasks, so that I know exactly what to do next.
  - **Acceptance criteria:** Each roadmap item includes skill, why it matters, current status, missing evidence, recommended task, project idea, Definition of Done, estimated effort, and milestone.
- As a user, I want project recommendations that close multiple skill gaps at once, so that I don't waste time on disconnected tutorials.
  - **Acceptance criteria:** Each generated project lists the skills it covers, a skill coverage score, difficulty, and estimated time.
- As a user, I want to mark roadmap tasks as Not Started / In Progress / Blocked / Completed / Verified, so that I can track my progress.
  - **Acceptance criteria:** Status changes are persisted; "Verified" can only be set automatically by the system (via evidence detection) or manually with a clear "self-reported" flag.

### GitHub Evidence Engine
- As a user, I want SkillGap to scan my public GitHub repositories, so that my evidence updates automatically as I build.
  - **Acceptance criteria:** Sync detects languages, frameworks, Dockerfiles, CI/CD workflows, tests, and README presence; sync respects GitHub API rate limits and shows last-synced timestamp.
- As a user, I want to manually trigger a re-sync, so that I can refresh evidence after finishing a project.
  - **Acceptance criteria:** Manual sync is rate-limited (e.g., once every N minutes) to avoid abuse.

### Readiness & Scoring
- As a user, I want to see multiple readiness scores instead of one vague percentage, so that I understand *why* I'm not ready.
  - **Acceptance criteria:** Dashboard shows Job Match, Skill Coverage, Evidence Strength, Portfolio Strength, and Production Readiness, each with a visible formula/explanation.
- As a user, I want a "Next Best Action" recommendation, so that I always know the single highest-value thing to do next.
  - **Acceptance criteria:** Recommendation is recalculated when roadmap state changes; recommendation includes a rationale referencing job relevance and gap severity.

### Interview Mode (Post-MVP feature, included for story completeness)
- As a user, I want interview questions generated from my own projects, so that I can prepare realistically.
  - **Acceptance criteria:** Questions reference specific technologies detected in the user's repositories; questions are not fabricated about skills without evidence.

