## 6. Non-Functional Requirements

- **Performance:** Dashboard initial load under 2s on cached data; AI-driven analyses (resume/job parsing) complete within 15s or return an async "processing" state with polling/webhook update.
- **Security:** All traffic over HTTPS; passwords hashed (bcrypt/argon2) if not using a managed auth provider; GitHub tokens encrypted at rest; least-privilege OAuth scopes.
- **Reliability:** Core read paths (dashboard, roadmap) must degrade gracefully if AI or GitHub services are down (show cached data instead of failing entirely).
- **Scalability:** Architecture must support moving background sync/AI jobs to a queue as user count grows, without a full rewrite (see Architecture §13).
- **Maintainability:** Layered backend (routes/services/repositories); AI prompts and schemas centralized and versioned.
- **Accessibility:** WCAG 2.1 AA color contrast on core dashboard views; keyboard navigability for primary flows; alt text for icons conveying status.
- **Usability:** No single onboarding step should require more than one page of input; extracted data always shown for user confirmation before being saved as fact.
- **Privacy:** Resume files and GitHub tokens are user-deletable; no cross-user data sharing; anonymized aggregate features (job market insight) opt-in only, post-MVP.
- **Observability:** Structured logs for AI calls (prompt version, latency, success/failure) and GitHub sync jobs; error tracking integrated (e.g., Sentry-equivalent) for both frontend and backend.

