## 7. Core User Flows

### Flow A — First-Time Onboarding to Roadmap
1. User signs up.
2. User creates a target job (title, description, optional company/deadline).
3. Job description analysis runs; user reviews extracted requirements.
4. User uploads resume and/or connects GitHub.
5. Resume/GitHub extraction runs; user reviews and confirms extracted skills/projects.
6. Skill Gap Engine computes status per skill.
7. Roadmap Engine generates roadmap items and project recommendations.
8. Dashboard shows readiness scores and Next Best Action.

### Flow B — GitHub Evidence Update Loop
1. User completes a recommended project locally and pushes to GitHub (adds Dockerfile, tests, CI workflow).
2. User triggers manual sync (or scheduled sync runs).
3. GitHub Integration detects new signals in the repository.
4. Evidence Engine updates evidence level/records for the affected skills.
5. Skill Gap Engine recalculates status; Roadmap Engine recalculates roadmap and readiness scores.
6. Dashboard reflects updated scores and "Recently Verified" list.

### Flow C — Comparing Multiple Target Jobs
1. User creates a second target job.
2. Both targets run through analysis independently.
3. User opens "Compare Jobs" view showing shared skills, unique skills, and per-job readiness.
4. User decides which target to prioritize based on shared-skill leverage.

